    { "id": "about", "type": "note", "at": [1, 0.6], "text": "Behavior yard: the engine's standard behaviors with no game module. Left, a side-view room: runner (hero-side, jumpHeight 2) starts beside the crate bin the spawner fills, jumps up through the one-way ledge, is lifted over the first gap by the updraft force area, rides the ferry platform over the second and reaches the goal sensor. A chain of three jointed links swings from chain-anchor. Right, a top-down room: walker (hero-top, maxSpeed 3) on seat 1, and courier, a nav agent on the walkway, which has a hole, with drop-point across it. Both heroes are camera targets: the one view follows their weighted centre, the runner at weight 1 and the walker at 0.1, so it starts on the runner with the crate bin in view; the walker's seat 1 waits for split screen." },
